2. Free community permission

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants you a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free copyright license to use, reproduce, run, modify, combine, display
and distribute the Software, in source or compiled form, for an eligible purpose.
This includes distributing precompiled applications and installers, creating
plugins and integrations, and developing and distributing meaningful new work.
You need not publish your modifications or pay a fee to the Licensor when your
purpose is eligible.

An eligible purpose is either:

(a) an individual's own personal use, learning, study, experimentation or hobby
    activity, not performed for or on behalf of an organization; or

(b) use for or on behalf of an organization whose Group Revenue is less than
    US$10,000,000. Eligible organizations may use the Software commercially.

For this license, an organization includes a company, sole proprietorship,
partnership, nonprofit or other organized entity. Its group includes all entities
that directly or indirectly control it, that it controls, or that share common
control with it. Control means ownership of more than half of the voting rights
or the power to direct management and policies by ownership, contract or otherwise.

Group Revenue is the combined gross revenue and equivalent gross receipts of
the group during the preceding twelve months, eliminating amounts counted more
than once solely because of transactions within the group. Convert non-US-dollar
amounts using the relevant central bank's published average exchange rate for
that period. Evaluate eligibility when use begins, at least annually thereafter,
and when ownership or control changes. A contractor, employee, subsidiary or
nominal individual cannot use personal or smaller-organization eligibility to
perform work for a group that is not eligible.

If your group reaches or exceeds the threshold, obtain the separate permission
in section 3 before further use for that group. Genuine personal use remains
eligible regardless of an individual's employer. There is no employee-count
limit and no automatic future conversion to a different license.

3. Separate paid permission for larger organizations

Use for or on behalf of a group with Group Revenue at or above US$10,000,000 is
not covered by the community grant. It requires a separate written commercial
agreement signed by the Licensor before that use. Contact the Licensor through
the public contact above. The Licensor may decline to offer an agreement; payment
alone does not create permission.

Commercial permission is separate from this community grant. It does not assign
ownership or grant exclusivity over the Software, and does not prevent the
Licensor from continuing free community development and distribution. No fee,
price, support commitment or other commercial term is established by this license.

